Data URL
A data URL is a URL that starts with 'data:'. It can be opened directly in your browser in the same way as opening a HTTP(S) URL. It can bypass most browser extensions running on Chromium-based browsers (including Chrome, Edge). It however cannot be used to bypass external network restrictions, as it uses embed code to embed the target website.


To use a data URL, copy the entire text starting from ‘data:’ and paste it into a new tab. Press enter to open the page.


Note: Data URLs are not immune to history logging, so you will need to delete history manually.


Version 1 (XML):
data:application/xml;base64,


Version 1 (HTML):
data:text/html;base64,


 Version 2 (SVG):
data:image/svg+xml;base64,


